commits.risk:
Low. Only landings whose link names a colour or item the page's stored copy lacks wait for Shopify, at most 3 seconds:
- on the published site, a colour or size added in Shopify since the latest publish (today: Aquarelle Rivière Bracelet's White and Pink links);
- on a page opened without its pre-drawn copy, every Star Point Band link except the plain page and its Gold US 6 ad;
- any link naming a colour the piece is not sold in.
A shopper who leaves the site in that time has the view sent as the page closes. The browser normally delivers it, but that could not be measured here. A shopper who taps through to another page of the shop in that time has the view sent at once, but Meta's server copy then names the new page as the page viewed (measured: Star Point Band's view named Woven Gold Hoops' page). On a page without its pre-drawn copy, the plain Star Point Band page and its Gold US 6 ad still report ₹999, the old price stored with the site (Audit C25); the published pre-drawn page reports ₹799. The Silver US 7 ad still opens on and reports US 6 (Audit C11). The old, unused product page still sends the lead variant.

